# Resolved by `op run` at the moment tofu starts, like ../op.env, and
# committed for the same reason: every op:// below is a REFERENCE, not a
# value. Vault, item and item-type are the contract; see ../../docs/CREDENTIALS.md.
#
#   op run --env-file=op.env -- tofu plan

# ─── Cloudflare ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The podcast's own token, NOT the one ../op.env resolves. That one is
# Zone > DNS > Edit, named opentofu-dns in Cloudflare, and it stays exactly
# that: a token that can repoint the mail should not be what a media pipeline
# runs on, and a token that can create buckets should not be able to repoint
# the mail. This one is Account > Workers R2 Storage > Edit and nothing else,
# which covers the buckets and the custom domain; Cloudflare writes the DNS
# record for a custom domain itself. Named opentofu-podcast in Cloudflare.
# API Credential item, so the field is `credential`.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=op://Engineering/Cloudflare podcast token/credential

# ─── R2, for the state backend only ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The same state bucket and the same tfstate token as ../op.env. It is
# OpenTofu's credential, not the podcast's, and it reaches the state bucket
# and nothing else. The token that writes the podcast's buckets is a third
# one, resolved by ../../tools/stage.env, and never comes near a tofu run.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=op://Engineering/R2 tfstate token/username
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=op://Engineering/R2 tfstate token/credential
